 "final_summary": "The bug was caused by incorrect cache key formatting in task deletion. The cache key for tasks is `task:ID`, but the deletion logic was using `task_id` directly. The fix updates the cache invalidation to use `f\"task:{task_id}\"`, ensuring the correct cache entry is invalidated after deletion. This prevents stale data from being returned and ensures a 404 response after deletion.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/services.py b/tracker/services.py\nindex f4a29cb..515d84e 100644\n--- a/tracker/services.py\n+++ b/tracker/services.py\n@@ -142,7 +142,7 @@ class TaskService:\n         if not auth.can_delete_task(user, task):\n             raise PermissionDeniedError(\"only the owner or an admin can delete this task\")\n         self.tasks.delete(task_id)\n-\n+        self.cache.invalidate(f\"task:{task_id}\")\n     # -- queries --------------------------------------------------------\n     def list_tasks(self, params):\n         page = parse_page_request(params, self.config)\n",
